# Android Architecture & Storage Standards

## MVVM Pattern
- Follow standard MVVM architectural structure with explicit separation between ViewModels and View layer data maps.
- ViewModels must expose state exclusively through an immutable backing property wrapping `StateFlow`.
- Collect flow flows safely on the UI view using `collectAsStateWithLifecycle()`.

## Dependency Injection (Hilt)
- Leverage Dagger Hilt for dependency injections across components.
- Declare dependencies targeting abstractions/interfaces rather than concrete implementations.
- Properly scope modules using `@InstallIn(ViewModelComponent::class)` or `@InstallIn(SingletonComponent::class)`.

## Database (Room)
- Utilize Room for all database layers, returning reactive data flows using `Flow<List<T>>`.
- Keep database operations abstract. Never fetch query operations synchronously on the UI thread.

# What to Avoid
- Do not use XML layouts — use Compose.
- Do not use LiveData — prefer StateFlow.
- Do not block the main thread.
- Do not use `!!` operator — handle nullability properly.

# Code Conventions
- Use Jetpack Compose for all UI — no XML layouts.
- Follow MVVM architecture with ViewModel and StateFlow.
- Use Hilt for dependency injection.
- Use Room for local database with Flow/StateFlow.
- Use Kotlin coroutines for async operations.
- Use Navigation Compose for screen navigation.
- Use Material 3 design components.
- Write UI previews with `@Preview` annotation.